<title>NEW ZEALAND: TABLE-NZ ADRs mostly firm as Dow rises again.</title>
<headline>TABLE-NZ ADRs mostly firm as Dow rises again.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were mostly firmer as the Dow Jones Industrial Index was up 35 points to 8096 in late New York trade at 7.50 a.m. NZT..</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S. and Australia.</p>
<p>Company     Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$28 09	  -0/09  *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$31/11	  +0/02  *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$21/13	  +0/01  *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$13	     +0/01  *</p>
<p>MAS Tech	 NASDAQ  US$17 5/8	 -0 1/2 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$39 0/1	 +0/13  *</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$16 3/8	 -0/01  *</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.38	    +0/02</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.86	    -0/02</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$1.44	    -0/01</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of eight shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
